course: dictionary
lesson: 6652
title: Numerals: writing numbers
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A numeral is a symbol that stands for a number. The digits we use every day, like 7, are numerals. So are Roman numerals, like VII, which also means seven. «Many clocks also have numbers, and old or fancy clocks may write them as Roman numerals.»
explain: Look at the words around a number to know what kind of numeral you are reading. «Write the answer in numerals» means use digits like 8, not the word eight. In a sentence, «seven» is a word for a number, and «7» is a numeral.
explain: The digits 0 to 9 are called Arabic numerals, even though they were first developed in India. «The digits 0 to 9 that we use were invented in India and passed on to Europe; they are often called Arabic numerals.» The name tells you how they reached Europe, not where they began.
fact: A numeral is a symbol or group of symbols that stands for a number.
fact: Arabic numerals are the digits 0 to 9 that we use most of the time.
fact: Roman numerals use letters: I is 1, V is 5, X is 10, L is 50, C is 100, D is 500 and M is 1000.
fact: «Roman numerals» are often seen on clocks, in book chapters and after kings' names, like Henry VIII.
fact: «Write in numerals» means use digits, not words: write 12, not twelve.
exercise: What is a numeral? | *A symbol or group of symbols that stands for a number | A shape with four sides | A word that names a colour | A letter of the alphabet
exercise: On a clock face, «Roman numerals» show X. What number is that? | *10 | 5 | 100 | 1
exercise: Which line uses numerals, not words? | *7 eggs | Seven eggs | Seven-hundred eggs | Seventh egg
test: Which Roman numeral means 50? | D | M | C | *L
test: Which of these is an Arabic numeral? | X | V | *9 | I
exam: Which Roman numeral means 1000? | X | C | D | *M
